Upstream-bound: no
Subject: [PORT_HOST] P7.7 test hooks: DW3_LANGUAGE, DW3_FORCE_FORM, DW3_FORCE_TECH, DW3_FORCE_STEAL, DW3_FORCE_HIT, DW3_FORCE_ENEMY_ITEM / _HP

Debug aids for the P7.7 replay scenarios, in the style of the P3.3 hooks
(DW3_FORCE_ENCOUNTER, DW3_FORCE_PARTY). All are read from the environment
under PORT_HOST and do nothing when unset, so a normal run and every
existing replay scenario are bit-identical. The Switch build has no
environment.

* DW3_LANGUAGE=<0-6> (EU only, newGame, before initNewGameData): sets LANGUAGE for a run
  that boots past the country select (2 English, 3 French, 5 German,
  4 Italian, 6 Spanish, the values of CNTY_SEL_languages), to look at the
  battle texts of each language.
* DW3_FORCE_FORM=<Digimon id> (WFIGHTMN addFighters): the first partner
  starts the battle as that Digimon, what the field menu's battle
  digivolution (Partner.battleDigivolve) does, e.g. 386 Dinohumon for
  Kotemon.
* DW3_FORCE_NICKNAME=<letters> (same place): the first partner is called that
  (GAME.partners[].info.name, what the Nickname Shop sets).
* DW3_FORCE_ENEMY_ITEM=<item> / DW3_FORCE_ENEMY_HP=<hp> (WFIGHTMN_initFighters):
  the first enemy holds that item and has that (max) HP.
* DW3_FORCE_TECH=<tech id> (FIGHTSTG_startTechAction): the partner's technique
  action uses that technique (127 Picking Claw, 128 Snapping Claw).
* DW3_FORCE_HIT=1 (FIGHTSTG_rollHit): the partner's techniques always hit.
* DW3_FORCE_STEAL=1 (FIGHTSTG_rollSteal): the steal roll of a partner
  technique succeeds, so a replay does not depend on the enemy's item chance.

